---
title: Example · Order schema
config:
  look: handDrawn
  handDrawnSeed: 5
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    mainBkg: "#333333"
    rowOdd: "#333333"
    rowEven: "#2a2a2a"
---
%% Attribute columns are fixed to type, name, key (`PK`/`FK`/`UK`), comment; the comment reads `description · e.g. value` (`설명 · 예: 값` in Korean text).
%% Cardinality, left end · right end: `||` exactly one · `|o` · `o|` zero or one · `}|` · `|{` one or more · `}o` · `o{` zero or more; word forms such as `one or zero`, `one or more`, `zero or many`, `1`, `0+` also work.
%% `subgraph Name … end` groups entities only in Mermaid 12; 11.16 draws `subgraph`, the name and `end` as extra entities.
%% `--` identifying (child key includes the parent's) · `..` non-identifying; word forms read `only one to zero or more` (`to` identifying) and `many(0) optionally to 1+` (`optionally to` non-identifying, dashed).
%% A `type?` marks a nullable column, `type[]` an array, `type(99)` a length; `name["Label"]` aliases an entity; `direction LR` and `class`/`:::` work as in flowcharts.
erDiagram
  direction LR
  customers {
    TEXT id PK "Customer identifier · e.g. cus_41f2"
    TEXT email UK "Login address · e.g. ana@example.com"
  }
  orders {
    TEXT id PK "Order identifier · e.g. ord_8f3a"
    TEXT customer_id FK "Buyer · e.g. cus_41f2"
    TEXT status "Lifecycle state · e.g. paid, shipped"
    TIMESTAMP? shipped_at "Hand-over time · e.g. 2026-05-01T09:30Z"
  }
  order_lines {
    TEXT order_id PK, FK "Owning order · e.g. ord_8f3a"
    INTEGER line_no PK "Position in the order · e.g. 1"
    TEXT product_sku FK "Ordered product · e.g. SKU-1009"
    INTEGER qty "Units · e.g. 2"
  }
  products {
    TEXT sku PK "Stock keeping unit · e.g. SKU-1009"
    INTEGER price_cents "Unit price · e.g. 1999"
  }
  payments {
    TEXT id PK "Payment identifier · e.g. pay_77c0"
    TEXT order_id FK, UK "Paid order · e.g. ord_8f3a"
  }
  coupons["coupons · campaign codes"] {
    TEXT code PK "Redeemable code · e.g. SPRING10"
  }
  customers ||..o{ orders : "places"
  orders ||--|{ order_lines : "contains"
  products ||..o{ order_lines : "appears in"
  orders ||..o| payments : "is paid by"
  orders many(0) optionally to many(0) coupons : "redeems"

  classDef em fill:#173d25,stroke:#86efac
  class orders em
